# Studio page template (standard)

Every new or converted manager/workspace page uses the **Studio template**, as on Blog Ideas Studio (`/generator/bulk-prompt`) and the Changelog page (`src/components/manager/changelog/ChangelogTabContent.tsx`, the reference implementation). Do not mount the three-band `UnifiedWorkspaceChrome` on new pages.

## Studio template anatomy

- **Full-bleed shell**: the page fills the workspace (`SEO_WORKSPACE_SHELL_CLASS` pattern: flex column, `min-h-0 flex-1`, `overflow-hidden`); no header bands above the content.
- **Slim in-body toolbar** (one fixed-height row, `h-11`): page identity (`icon` + `title`) and page flags on the **left**; live status in the **middle** (`tabular-nums`, truncated, reserved width); **right** = secondary actions, then the primary run action (green `Button variant="run"`, like the studio's Ideas button). Reserve the action slots so nothing shifts while a run is active.
- **Controls live in the body**: filters, compose fields, and option clusters sit in the work area (left dock plus main pane), not in a black toolbar band. Panes own their scroll; the page itself does not scroll as a whole.
- **Green right rail** (SEO / Details / Agents / Assist) is shell-level and untouched; progress and detail surfaces publish there, or into the body panes, instead of a progress band.
- **Type floor**: 1rem everywhere (see `typography-min-1rem.mdc`). Flat wells (`bg-zinc-900`), no decorative borders, no nested frames, no stacked labels (see `flat-inline-forms.mdc`).

## Do not

- Mount `UnifiedWorkspaceChrome` on a new or converted page.
- Let conditional toolbar controls change the toolbar height (zero CLS, see `minimal-stacking-zero-cls.mdc`).
- Invent a one-off page chrome; copy the Studio composition from the reference implementations.

## Reference implementations

- Changelog (reference): `src/components/manager/changelog/ChangelogTabContent.tsx`
- Blog Ideas Studio: `/generator/bulk-prompt` (`BulkBlogGenerationTab`, `BulkPromptComposePanel`)

## Legacy: UnifiedWorkspaceChrome (existing pages only)

Pages that still mount `UnifiedWorkspaceChrome` (`src/components/shared/UnifiedWorkspaceChrome.tsx`) keep working; do not rip it out as a drive-by. When such a page is next touched for real work, migrate it to the Studio template. The three-band contract stays documented so legacy code remains readable:

| Band | Surface | Left | Right |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 Title | `bg-zinc-900/50` | `icon` + `title` + optional `titleRowMenu` | `titleRowEnd` |
| 2 Toolbar | `bg-black` | Options, filters, flyouts, selects | Main actions (`ml-auto`) |
| 3 Progress | `bg-zinc-900/50` | `progressLeading` + micro progress bar | (Details lives in the right sidebar) |

On legacy pages, keep heights aligned with the exported band classes (`UNIFIED_TITLE_BAND_CLASS`, `UNIFIED_TOOLBAR_CLASS`, `UNIFIED_PROGRESS_BAND_CLASS`) and `bulk-workspace-header-styles.ts` (`BULK_HEADER_*`). Legacy references: `OverviewContentHeader` (`overview-tab/OverviewMetaWorkspaceBar.tsx`), `SitemapOptimizerUnifiedHeader.tsx`, `DashboardWorkspaceHeader.tsx`, `BulkCsvWorkspaceHeader.tsx`, `BulkPromptWorkspaceHeader.tsx`.
